e, we are not suggesting that the quality scores of this framework are competitive with state-of-the-art denoisers. Currently, the main advantage is substantial speed. Tensorflow (Abadi et al., 2016) implementation converges in about 1700 iterations in an average of 14.29 seconds on a laptop GPU (NVIDIA GeForce GTX Ti 1650 with 4GB video memory) and 2.01 minutes on i-7 CPU. Pytorch (Paszke et al., 2019) implementation training converges in 40 epochs on average in 30.73 seconds on a GPU NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2080 Ti, and 2.73 minutes on i-7 CPU. Inference takes \u223c500 msec. For reference, RED-SD takes 15-20 minutes of processing for each image, on a CPU."
